+#!/usr/bin/env node
+/**
+ * THE PENCIL VERBS GATE (T9-W7 §13).  `npm run lint:verbs`
+ *
+ * Motion in this product is named by what a hand does on paper. This reads every shipped
+ * `transition:` and `animation:` under `src/` and asks eight things of it.
+ *
+ *   1′ A VERB        outside a `@keyframes` body a `transition:` curve is `var(--verb-*-ease)`
+ *                    or a `v-bind`. `--ease-*` is the SHAPE layer: legal as
+ *                    `animation-timing-function` inside a keyframe, or on an `animation:`
+ *                    the ledger admits as `shape`. A browser keyword is a red either way.
+ *   2  A RUNG        the DURATION — the first time value in a term — is a named rung
+ *                    (`var(--motion-*)`, another bound token like `--refuse-dur`, or a
+ *                    `v-bind`). A number typed at the call site is a red. No verb owns a
+ *                    number any more: every length is the ladder's.
+ *   2′ THE FENCE     the second and later time values are DELAYS. A delay is a wait, not a
+ *                    gesture: it keeps its own number and may not read a rung. This is the
+ *                    rule that gives the toggle's beats back — pass 1 spelled ten delays as
+ *                    rungs and moved six decided beats doing it.
+ *   3  THE SET       a term may only spend a rung its verb is allowed to spend.
+ *   5  THE PROPERTY  what a declaration MOVES is a subset of its verb's props, through the
+ *                    alias table. For an `animation:` the moved set is read from the
+ *                    `@keyframes` body, so a verb is enforced by what it does, not by taste.
+ *   5b DIRECTION     a keyframe whose end pose REDUCES coverage is a LEAVE and takes
+ *                    lift/rubOut; one that restores it is an ARRIVAL and takes
+ *                    layDown/writeIn. Keyframes are enforced; a transition is read only
+ *                    where the estate's own names carry the direction (`.is-active`,
+ *                    `-enter-active`, `-leave-active`, `.is-leaving`, `.is-rubbing-out`).
+ *   6  THE LEDGER    a row the rules cannot take is ADMITTED below with a KIND, a ruling AND
+ *                    THE RULES THAT RULING COVERS. The key is `${file} :: ${declaration} #${n}`
+ *                    — an occurrence ordinal, so two identical declarations in one file are two
+ *                    rows. Closed three ways: an admission whose site has gone is a red, and so
+ *                    is an offence the ruling does not name.
+ *   7  THE MOVERS,   every `.animate(` options object spends a verb: a `spend(` call, a spread
+ *      AND THE DOOR  of one, or a pass-through; a typed duration or a quoted curve there is the
+ *                    red. And every `spend(verb, rung)` spends a rung that verb is allowed to
+ *                    spend. The walk reads `.ts` AND `.vue` `<script>` blocks, because a script
+ *                    is code wherever it is written.
+ *   8  THE BEATS     `DarkModeToggle.vue` carries its gesture's beat table as data beside the
+ *                    gesture (`@toggle-beats`). Read BOTH ways: every beat must read back off
+ *                    the rule it names, and every `!important` transition/delay in that file's
+ *                    <style> outside the reduce block must be named by a beat. The record
